{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"id":"JGraph.Draw","latestVersion":"32.6.10","media":{"icons":[{"mimeType":"image/png","path":"media/icon.c2192d5b.png","priority":1,"sha256":"c2192d5bb1fce2c02c570222803e1892f6190848297b1e5c386b97d380647def","source":"winget-legacy"}],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"author":"JGraph Limited","copyright":"© 2005-2026 JGraph Ltd, Artisans' House, 7 Queensbridge, NN4 7BF, Northampton, England. Company","copyrightUrl":"https://www.diagrams.net/trust","description":"A diagramming desktop app based on Electron that wraps the core draw.io editor.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Documentation","DocumentUrl":"https://www.drawio.com/docs/"},{"DocumentLabel":"Wiki","DocumentUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop/wiki"}],"license":"GPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"author":"JGraph Limited","copyright":"© 2005-2026 JGraph Ltd, Artisans' House, 7 Queensbridge, NN4 7BF, Northampton, England. Company","copyrightUrl":"https://www.diagrams.net/trust","description":"A diagramming desktop app based on Electron that wraps the core draw.io editor.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Documentation","DocumentUrl":"https://www.drawio.com/docs/"},{"DocumentLabel":"Wiki","DocumentUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop/wiki"}],"license":"GPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","name":"draw.io","packageUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop","privacyUrl":"https://www.diagrams.net/trust","publisher":"JGraph","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop/issues","publisherUrl":"https://www.drawio.com/","releaseNotes":"ChangeLog:\n- Uses electron 44.10.2\n- Exports all pages as one SVG with --all-pages -f svg, with a view for each page, so that file.svg#Page-2 in an image shows the second page [jgraph/drawio#5821]\n- Stops the command line export from hanging on malformed PNG files\n- Updates to draw.io core 32.6.10. All changes from 32.6.1 to 32.6.10 are added in this build.\nTesting:\nVerified against the packaged, signed macOS build. Windows and Linux packages were verified from the produced release artifacts, their sizes and update manifests, rather than by running them.\nBase checks\n- Launch, open a file passed on the command line, add and edit shapes, change styles, undo and redo, copy and paste, save and reopen, insert, rename and delete pages, and zoom\n- Export to PNG and PDF from the app, and to PNG, JPEG, SVG, PDF, XML and HTML from the command line, covering scale, border, transparency, cropping, page selection with -p and --size page\n- Diagram round trip in an exported PDF, including reopening the exported PDF and recovering both pages\n- Mermaid and CSV import, and the --layout and --normalize options from the command line\n- Shape search, stencils and shape libraries, and the export, print and Page Setup dialogs\n- Settings and the window position and size survive a restart\n- The Quick Look extension is registered for this build, sandboxed and separately signed\n- The macOS bundle is signed with a Developer ID certificate under the hardened runtime, is notarised and stapled\n- The Electron security fuses are applied\n- 296 unit tests pass\nAll pages as one SVG\n- A file with 2 pages exports one SVG with a view for the name and the ID of each page, and in a browser the views show the second page and no view shows the first page\n- A file with 3000 pages exports in about 6 seconds with all of its views\n- A page with math, a page with a traced image and the page after them all arrive in the SVG\n- The Alt Text of each page is written as its title with markup escaped, and pages without one have none\nMalformed PNG files\n- Five crafted PNG files, each in a folder export and as a listed file with -f html, end without hanging, and the good diagram next to them is still exported. Three of them hung the previous release on both paths\n- A PNG with an embedded diagram is still found by a folder export, and a PNG without one is skipped\nChecks around the changes\n- Edges with the outline perimeter end on the outline of an image in SVG and PDF exports, also for the PDF export of a .drawio.svg file\n- Relative links in SVG exports are written without the install path, and javascript: links lose their scheme\n- A .mmd file with a title and description opens with them as the Alt Text of the page, and SVG exports write them as the title\n- Opening a diagram with a data source makes no request, and file URLs are refused as data sources\n- Alt+Shift+D describes the selection and Alt+Shift+U opens the text outline\n- Three library saves without a dialog each reach the file, and drafts are written next to the file and read back\n- Reads, stats and writes of paths the user has not authorised are still refused [GHSA-fjgc-8xgj-rvh4]\n- file: and javascript: links are not opened externally\n- The File menu and the Export as menu have the same entries as 32.6.1\n- All 5 update manifests name this version, with matching sizes","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop/releases/tag/v32.6.10","tags":["chart","design","diagram","draw","gantt","graph","graphics","mind-map","mind-mapping","mindmap","uml"]},"zh-CN":{"description":"一款基于 Electron 的图表设计桌面应用，封装了核心 draw.io 编辑器。","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Wiki","DocumentUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop/wiki"},{"DocumentLabel":"文档","DocumentUrl":"https://www.drawio.com/docs/"}],"locale":"zh-CN","tags":["uml","图形","图示","图表","思维导图","甘特图","绘图","脑图","设计"]}},"name":"draw.io","packageUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop","privacyUrl":"https://www.diagrams.net/trust","publisher":"JGraph","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop/issues","publisherUrl":"https://www.drawio.com/","releaseNotes":"ChangeLog:\n- Uses electron 44.10.2\n- Exports all pages as one SVG with --all-pages -f svg, with a view for each page, so that file.svg#Page-2 in an image shows the second page [jgraph/drawio#5821]\n- Stops the command line export from hanging on malformed PNG files\n- Updates to draw.io core 32.6.10. All changes from 32.6.1 to 32.6.10 are added in this build.\nTesting:\nVerified against the packaged, signed macOS build. Windows and Linux packages were verified from the produced release artifacts, their sizes and update manifests, rather than by running them.\nBase checks\n- Launch, open a file passed on the command line, add and edit shapes, change styles, undo and redo, copy and paste, save and reopen, insert, rename and delete pages, and zoom\n- Export to PNG and PDF from the app, and to PNG, JPEG, SVG, PDF, XML and HTML from the command line, covering scale, border, transparency, cropping, page selection with -p and --size page\n- Diagram round trip in an exported PDF, including reopening the exported PDF and recovering both pages\n- Mermaid and CSV import, and the --layout and --normalize options from the command line\n- Shape search, stencils and shape libraries, and the export, print and Page Setup dialogs\n- Settings and the window position and size survive a restart\n- The Quick Look extension is registered for this build, sandboxed and separately signed\n- The macOS bundle is signed with a Developer ID certificate under the hardened runtime, is notarised and stapled\n- The Electron security fuses are applied\n- 296 unit tests pass\nAll pages as one SVG\n- A file with 2 pages exports one SVG with a view for the name and the ID of each page, and in a browser the views show the second page and no view shows the first page\n- A file with 3000 pages exports in about 6 seconds with all of its views\n- A page with math, a page with a traced image and the page after them all arrive in the SVG\n- The Alt Text of each page is written as its title with markup escaped, and pages without one have none\nMalformed PNG files\n- Five crafted PNG files, each in a folder export and as a listed file with -f html, end without hanging, and the good diagram next to them is still exported. Three of them hung the previous release on both paths\n- A PNG with an embedded diagram is still found by a folder export, and a PNG without one is skipped\nChecks around the changes\n- Edges with the outline perimeter end on the outline of an image in SVG and PDF exports, also for the PDF export of a .drawio.svg file\n- Relative links in SVG exports are written without the install path, and javascript: links lose their scheme\n- A .mmd file with a title and description opens with them as the Alt Text of the page, and SVG exports write them as the title\n- Opening a diagram with a data source makes no request, and file URLs are refused as data sources\n- Alt+Shift+D describes the selection and Alt+Shift+U opens the text outline\n- Three library saves without a dialog each reach the file, and drafts are written next to the file and read back\n- Reads, stats and writes of paths the user has not authorised are still refused [GHSA-fjgc-8xgj-rvh4]\n- file: and javascript: links are not opened externally\n- The File menu and the Export as menu have the same entries as 32.6.1\n- All 5 update manifests name this version, with matching sizes","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop/releases/tag/v32.6.10","tags":["chart","design","diagram","draw","gantt","graph","graphics","mind-map","mind-mapping","mindmap","uml"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/32.6.10/app.json","detailSha256":"59948d3567668072dfe8d4c0bb7a80d174c38f1365ad1318eef283eefb57d75e","releaseDate":"2026-11-04","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"32.6.10"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/32.6.1/app.json","detailSha256":"b19aca9f22e85a691bc1cca94df6d48841964b68607b49ad40e0c21a7a86ac14","releaseDate":"2026-10-23","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"32.6.1"},{"architectures":["